Your Hospital Admin dashboard works like this:

You log in at /hospital/login with hospital admin credentials.
Frontend calls POST /api/auth/hospital/login.
On success, it stores:
hospitalToken (JWT)
hospital (user object)
Protected routing checks that token is valid and role is hospital_admin; otherwise it sends you back to login.
What the dashboard loads
When /hospital/dashboard opens, it calls two APIs:

GET /api/hospital/metrics
GET /api/hospital/alerts/recent
Metrics shown on cards
From metrics, it shows:

Registered patients
Consultation count
Adherence log count
Avg adherence (last 7 days)
Open alerts
Dropout risk count
These are calculated on the backend using MongoDB aggregations, scoped to the admin’s hospital.

Recent Alerts table
From alerts/recent, it shows:

Date
Patient
Severity (low/medium/high)
Alert reason/message
Status (open/resolved logic)
Real-time behavior
Dashboard joins Socket room hospital and listens for:

alert:new
consultation:new
adherence:updated
When these events arrive, it auto-refreshes metrics + recent alerts, so the dashboard stays near real-time.

Other hospital admin pages (same token/session)
Inside hospital area, admin can also use:

/hospital/staff
list doctors (GET /api/hospital/doctors)
create doctor with temp password (POST /api/hospital/doctors)
create one-time patient invite link (POST /api/hospital/patient-invites)
/hospital/patients and /hospital/patients/:id
/hospital/alerts
/hospital/reports
exports CSV for patients and alerts
So in short: Hospital admin dashboard is an authenticated, hospital-scoped operations view that combines KPI metrics + risk alerts + staff/report workflows, with real-time refresh from Socket.IO events.



